an4.32:4.1 starts: But because the wise show regard
an4.32:4.2 starts: for these bonds of fellowship,
an4.32:4.3 starts: they achieve greatness
an4.32:4.4 starts: and are praised.
an4.50:10.1 starts: drink alcohol & fermented liquor,
an4.50:10.2 starts: engage in sexual intercourse,
an4.50:10.3 starts: unwise,
# superseded: an4.50:10.4 starts: consent to gold & silver,
# superseded: an4.50:10.5 starts: live by means of wrong livelihood
# superseded: an4.50:10.6 starts: —some brahmans & contemplatives.
an4.52:7.1 starts: So conviction & virtue,
an4.52:7.2 starts: confidence & Dhamma-vision
an4.52:7.3 starts: should be cultivated by the intelligent,
an4.52:7.4 starts: remembering the Buddhas’ teachings.’”
an4.33:3.1 starts: When the Awakened One, through direct knowledge,
an4.33:3.2 starts: —the Teacher, the person with no peer
an4.33:3.3 starts: in the world with its devas—
an4.33:3.4 starts: sets the Dhamma wheel rolling:
an4.34:5.1 starts: With
an4.34:5.2 starts: realizing the supreme Dhamma
an4.34:5.3 starts: confidence in the supreme Buddha,
an4.34:5.4 starts: unsurpassed
an4.35:6.1 starts: He who, knowing, declared
an4.35:6.2 starts: from the snare of death,
an4.35:6.3 starts: welfare
an4.35:6.4 starts: the methodical Dhamma—
an4.35:6.5 starts: seeing & hearing which,
an4.35:6.6 starts: many people grow clear & calm;
an4.35:7.1 starts: who is skilled in what is &
an4.35:7.2 starts: his task done, effluent-free:
an4.35:7.3 starts: is called
an4.35:7.4 starts: bearing his last body,
an4.36:5.1 starts: “The effluents by which I would go
an4.36:5.2 starts: to a deva-state,
an4.36:5.3 starts: or become a gandhabba in the sky,
an4.36:5.4 starts: or go to a yakkha-state & human-state:
an4.36:5.5 starts: Those have been destroyed by me,
an4.36:5.6 starts: ruined, their stems removed.
an4.38:6.1 starts: Through the relinquishing of searches
an4.38:6.2 starts: & the abolishing of viewpoints
an4.38:6.3 starts: of one dispassionate to
an4.38:6.4 starts: and released in the ending
an4.42:4.1 starts: hard to overcome, hard to beat,
an4.42:4.2 starts: profound, hard to defeat.
an4.42:4.3 starts: He knows what’s worthwhile
an4.42:4.4 starts: proficient in (recognizing) both,
an4.45:7.1 starts: It’s not to be reached by traveling,
an4.45:7.2 starts: the end of the cosmos—
an4.45:7.3 starts: And it’s not without reaching
an4.45:7.4 starts: that there is release
an4.55:4.1 starts: Husband & wife, both of them
an4.55:4.2 starts: being restrained,
an4.55:4.3 starts: living by the Dhamma,
an4.55:4.4 starts: addressing each other
